message: "If you use or discuss this repository, please cite it as below."
title: >-
  Rainich-Kaluza reconstruction: third-order non-identifiability and
  fourth-order recovery of the Einstein-Maxwell-dilaton coupling square
  from metric jets
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kehoe
    given-names: James
repository-code: "https://github.com/jimpeebles/rainich-kaluza-reconstruction"
license: MIT
version: 0.3.0-dev
date-released: 2026-08-14
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - Mathlib
  - formalized mathematics
  - general relativity
  - Rainich theory
  - Kaluza-Klein
  - Einstein-Maxwell-dilaton
  - inverse problems
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of a sharp metric-jet identifiability
  threshold for the Einstein-Maxwell-dilaton coupling square on an active,
  non-null, simple-spectrum branch: the metric three-jet cannot identify
  the coupling (the ambiguity is an exact one-parameter shear orbit), while
  a finite fourth-order metric-only detector recovers it, with the Kaluza
  value 3 as a necessary selector. Includes an exact-arithmetic validation
  suite and a claim ledger separating machine-checked, human/external,
  exact-symbolic, and open claims.
